; A `;@axiom:` line inside a `#| ... |#` block comment is comment text,
; not metadata. The lexer's AXTAG pass is a SECOND walk over the source
; - it does not read the token stream - so it has to skip exactly what
; tokenization skips, and a block comment is now one of those things.
;
; The two functions below are the same function twice: same body, same
; `pure` claim, same contradiction. The only difference is that one
; claim is inside a block comment. Exactly one AX3010 is correct. A
; scanner that missed the block comment would report two, at different
; lines, which is what makes this a fixture and not a file with an
; empty golden.
(:: quiet (-> Int Int))

#|
;@axiom:pure
|#
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (quiet fd)
  {
    (__syscall3 1 fd 0 0)
    0
  }
)

(:: loud (-> Int Int))

;@axiom:pure
(fn (loud fd)
  {
    (__syscall3 1 fd 0 0)
    0
  }
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
